    Comment why amoalu selects the word compare when Zabha is disabled
    
    Answers a review question on #1877: without Zabha the byte and halfword AMO
    encodings are illegal and never reach the LSU, so those two case arms are
    don't-cares.  Selecting lt32 rather than lt8/lt16 there is a synthesis
    optimization, leaving the narrow signed-compare muxes with no consumer so the
    tool can trim them.  No functional change.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

