Author: David Harris <David_Harris@hmc.edu>
Date:   Tue Sep 15 21:20:17 2026 -0700

    Enable Zabha in the ImperasDV lockstep configs
    
    Add cpu/Zabha=T to the rv64gc and rv32gc imperas.ic files so lockstep
    accepts the byte and halfword AMOs.
    
    Without the override ImperasDV decodes those encodings as vector
    instructions and reports an illegal instruction, so lockstep diverges on
    the first byte AMO. Verified on rv64gc and rv32gc: amoadd.b, amomin.b,
    amominu.b, amoswap.h, amomax.h and amomaxu.h all run with zero mismatches.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

